128
00:14:19,822 --> 00:14:23,682
ボカロ歌おうかなと思って。うん。
I thought I'd sing a Vocaloid song. Yep.

129
00:14:24,742 --> 00:14:35,722
わしはね、わしはね、あちちめらはね、ボカロが大好き！ボカロイドが大好き！音声合成が大好き！
As for me, as for me, Atsuchi Mela loves Vocaloid! I love Vocaloids! I love speech synthesis!

130
00:14:36,682 --> 00:14:51,602
ということもね、ボカロ曲も歌おうかなと思って、あのー、なんか、やっぱ収益化記念？記念じゃし、あのー、なんか、
So I thought I'd sing some Vocaloid songs too, you know, since it's a monetization celebration... and commemorate it, and...

131
00:14:51,742 --> 00:15:01,702
節目っぽい人の歌おうかなと思って、早い？まだ1ヶ月経ってないの早いかな？早いかなと思ったんじゃけど、なんか、あのー、ぐわってなるやつ歌おうか...
I thought about singing a song that feels like a milestone, but is it too early? It hasn't even been a month yet, is that too early? I thought it might be, but you know, I wanted to sing something that hits you right in the feels...

132
00:15:02,160 --> 00:15:06,640
なあって思って、そう、泣いちゃうやつ歌おうかなって思って。
I was thinking, yeah, I'd sing something that makes you cry.

133
00:15:09,030 --> 00:15:11,950
歌おうと、おもいますのじゃー！
So I'm gonna sing it, noja!

134
00:15:12,780 --> 00:15:17,400
えこ、忘れずに。のじゃー！
Don't forget the echo. Noja!

135
00:15:19,430 --> 00:15:25,730
アトラクトライトという曲を、歌いますのじゃー。
I'll be singing a song called Attract Light, noja.

136
00:15:26,200 --> 00:15:31,020
うん、ぐわってなるやつ。ぐわってなるやつ。
Yeah, the kind of song that hits you right in the feels. The kind that really gets to you.

137
00:15:32,380 --> 00:15:35,490
あ、これ原曲も大好きだからお前らも聞いてほしいな。
Ah, I love the original version too, so I want you guys to listen to it as well.

138
00:15:37,430 --> 00:15:48,580
今日は、泣かしに行こうと思って。あの見守ってくれてたお前らを泣かしに行こうと思って、こっから後2曲も泣かせる気しかないからね、お前らのこと。
Today, I thought I'd go make you cry. I thought I'd go make you guys cry since you've been watching over me, and from here on, for the last two songs, I'm only planning to make you cry, you guys.

139
00:15:50,370 --> 00:15:56,930
じゃあ、歌いますのじゃー。え、アトラクトライトという曲を歌いますのじゃー！よいしょ。
Well then, I'll sing, noja. Um, I'll sing a song called Attract Light, noja! Here we go.

140
00:16:11,564 --> 00:16:15,244
まだ青くって拙い もろくって足りない
Still too green and clumsy, fragile and lacking,

141
00:16:15,664 --> 00:16:20,194
小さくて弱くてどうしようもない僕だ
so small and weak and helpless am I.

142
00:16:32,454 --> 00:16:36,294
知りたかったんだ 成功と失敗 マルとバツの
I wanted to know the difference between success and failure, circles and crosses,

143
00:16:36,654 --> 00:16:43,784
今日を境界線を引くとしたら どこだろう
if we were to draw the boundary line for today, where would it be?

144
00:16:43,784 --> 00:16:50,694
それじゃあバツがマルになって 失敗を乗り越えたとしたら
So if crosses turned into circles and we overcame failure,

145
00:16:50,694 --> 00:16:56,474
それを何と呼ぶんだ いつか名前をつけよう
what would we call that? Let's give it a name someday.

146
00:16:56,474 --> 00:17:00,824
夢は叶わない 願いは届かない
Dreams won't come true, wishes won't reach,

147
00:17:01,084 --> 00:17:06,184
だから歩くのをやめてしまうのか
so is that why we stop walking?

148
00:17:06,424 --> 00:17:10,834
努力は報われない 誰も認めてくれない
Effort isn't rewarded, no one acknowledges us,

149
00:17:11,014 --> 00:17:18,934
だから走るのをやめてしまうのか 止まってしまうのか やめてしまいたい
so is that why we stop running? Stop completely? Want to just give up?

150
00:17:19,434 --> 00:17:26,494
理由なら10も100も1000もあった でもその全てがちっぽけに見える
There were ten, a hundred, a thousand reasons, yet all of them looked so trivial,

151
00:17:26,494 --> 00:17:32,264
一つがあった 逃げ出すための言葉なら 飽きるほど浮かんだ
but there was one thing: if it were words to run away from, enough floated up to grow tired of,

152
00:17:32,264 --> 00:17:38,614
でもそれを壊さないだけの輝きがあった
yet there was a brilliance that kept me from breaking it.

153
00:17:42,894 --> 00:17:47,424
知りたかったんだ 明日と今日の
I wanted to know the boundary line between tomorrow and today,

154
00:17:47,714 --> 00:17:54,584
大人と子どもの境界線を引くとしたら どこだろう
between adults and children, if we were to draw it, where would it be?

155
00:17:54,584 --> 00:18:01,494
大人になったら 誰に成りたいって みんな言うけれど
When we become adults, everyone says who they want to become,

156
00:18:01,744 --> 00:18:07,454
じゃあ何にもなれないんだろうか 今日の僕は
then is today's me unable to become anything at all?

157
00:18:07,734 --> 00:18:15,234
三年前誰かが 夕空に投げた言い訳は
The excuse someone threw into the evening sky three years ago,

158
00:18:15,234 --> 00:18:21,504
もう忘れた 必要のない言葉だ
I've already forgotten it, it's unnecessary words.

159
00:18:21,704 --> 00:18:26,364
いつか口ずさむ 歌にでもしよう
Let's turn it into a song to hum someday.

160
00:18:26,624 --> 00:18:33,834
道しるべなんてない 誰も教えてくれない だから足跡は
There are no signposts, no one teaches us, so our footsteps crossed

161
00:18:33,834 --> 00:18:40,294
交わったんだ 出会えたんだ 壊してしまいたい夜なら
and met, and if it's a night we want to destroy,

162
00:18:40,294 --> 00:18:47,064
10も100も1000もあった でもその全て飛び越える
there were ten, a hundred, a thousand, yet to leap over all of them,

163
00:18:47,064 --> 00:18:53,694
羽を持っていたんだ あの日始まった物語は
I had wings! The story that began on that day,

164
00:18:53,694 --> 00:19:01,254
どこに向かうんだろうか 明日からの僕に 宿題が増えたみたいだ
where is it heading? It's as if homework has increased for me starting tomorrow.

165
00:19:16,414 --> 00:19:24,294
横一列でスタートを切った あの日の僕らはもういない
The version of us who started off in a single file line on that day is no longer here.

166
00:19:24,294 --> 00:19:33,684
君の行く場所に 僕の行く場所に それぞれは必要ないから
Because your destination and my destination don't need each other,

167
00:19:33,684 --> 00:19:41,034
いくつもの挫折を超えて いくつもの冬を超えて
overcoming numerous setbacks, overcoming numerous winters,

168
00:19:41,034 --> 00:19:47,514
花が開くように 青い宝石が輝くように
so that flowers bloom, so that blue jewels shine,

169
00:19:47,514 --> 00:19:54,454
だって見つけたんだ 眩しくって仕方がないんだ
because I found it, it's so blinding I can't help it,

170
00:19:54,454 --> 00:19:58,284
この光の正体は
the true nature of this light is...

171
00:19:58,364 --> 00:20:05,038
ああ やめてしまいたい 理由なら10も100も1000もあった でもその全てがちっぽけに見えたのは
Ah, if it's reasons to want to give up, there were ten, a hundred, a thousand, yet why did all of them look so trivial...

172
00:20:44,196 --> 00:20:51,936
のじゃー！アトラクトライトでしたのじゃー！
Noja~! That was "Attract Light"~!

173
00:20:53,166 --> 00:20:58,526
どなたやら感動してきたんじゃない？
Weren't you guys moved by now?

174
00:20:58,526 --> 00:21:03,546
わしの歌に泣けてきたんじゃないそろそろ？感動してきたじゃん...
Didn't my song make you cry? You were so moved...

175
00:21:04,046 --> 00:21:07,566
って何じゃ、もう20分なのじゃ？笑った、笑ったじゃない！
Wait, it's already been 20 minutes? You laughed, you laughed at me!

176
00:21:10,546 --> 00:21:15,046
えっと...歌いますのじゃー！まずいの一、え、まずくない？時間！
Um... I'm gonna sing~! Oh no, wait, isn't that bad? The time!

177
00:21:20,246 --> 00:21:27,546
焦ってるのじゃ焦ってるのじゃ、待って待って、どっと焦り、わしどっと焦り、どっと焦りしてる...
I'm panicking, I'm panicking, wait, wait, I'm panicking so much, I'm totally panicking...

178
00:21:28,246 --> 00:21:32,546
よし、次の曲いきますのじゃー！聞いてください！
Alright, time for the next song~! Please listen!

179
00:21:33,646 --> 00:21:34,946
Wishing！
"Wishing"!

180
00:22:00,896 --> 00:22:11,146
朝になったら ふたり 手を合わせて
When morning comes, the two of us join hands together...

181
00:22:13,196 --> 00:22:24,246
他愛ないこと 少しお話ししたいな
...and talk a little about silly everyday things.

182
00:22:26,146 --> 00:22:37,946
晴れた午後を そっと 手をつないで
Hand in hand, gently walking through a sunny afternoon...

183
00:22:38,896 --> 00:22:49,946
穏やかな 街を 少し 歩いてみたい
...I want to walk a little through a peaceful town.

184
00:22:51,046 --> 00:23:02,246
そんな想像さえ 移動したくて
Just imagining that makes me want to move...

185
00:23:03,146 --> 00:23:19,146
いつまでも 同じ時間を 一緒に過ごしたくて
...because I want to spend the exact same time together with you forever.

186
00:23:21,096 --> 00:23:35,046
だって 朝も 夜も 伝えたいこと たくさんがあって
Because whether morning or night, there are so many things I want to tell you!

187
00:23:36,046 --> 00:23:50,296
今日も 明日も 好きだなんて 言えたら...
If I could just say "I love you" today and tomorrow too...

188
00:23:55,546 --> 00:24:12,546
リゼロの、挿入歌のキャラクターソングレスのじゃ、レムが歌ってる曲ですのじゃ。
That's the insert character song from Re:Zero, the song sung by Rem.

189
00:24:15,146 --> 00:24:28,046
夜になったら 星の見える場所で 眠りに着くまで ずっと寄り添いたいな
"When night falls, I want to snuggle up close to you in a place where the stars are visible, until we fall asleep."

190
00:24:28,446 --> 00:24:39,546
触れられる距離が 愛おしくて その声を その対応を もっと感じて
"The distance where we can touch is so precious; I want to feel your voice and your responses even more..."

191
00:24:40,046 --> 00:24:53,046
触れられる距離が 愛おしくて その声を その対応を もっと感じて...えたら！
"...if I could just reach them!"

192
00:25:04,454 --> 00:25:09,314
溢れて
Overflowing,

193
00:25:10,314 --> 00:25:14,254
だって 何度も
Over and over, calling...

194
00:25:15,054 --> 00:25:24,254
何度も名前を呼んで もまだ足りなくて
...calling your name, and still it's not enough.

195
00:25:24,814 --> 00:25:33,994
今日も明日も ふたりで あーいれたら
If today and tomorrow, the two of us could be together...

196
00:25:40,694 --> 00:25:50,994
切ないときはきれいだな 花を飾りましょう
When times are painful, let's decorate with flowers.

197
00:25:54,174 --> 00:26:03,174
悲しいときは楽しい お話をしましょう
When times are sad, let's talk about happy things.

198
00:26:09,254 --> 00:26:19,714
神様に おねだり ただ触ってくれるだけで
Begging the gods, just having you touch me...

199
00:26:25,214 --> 00:26:33,274
心も瞬間 明るくなる
...makes my heart instantly brighten up.

200
00:26:33,814 --> 00:26:46,634
だって朝も夜も叶えたいことこんなにあって
Because there are so many things I want to make come true, morning and night.

201
00:26:47,274 --> 00:26:56,414
今日も明日も幸せだと あー言えたら
If I could say today and tomorrow are happy...

202
00:27:04,694 --> 00:27:12,134
いいのに
That would be wonderful.

203
00:27:12,634 --> 00:27:26,634
ウィッシングでしたのじゃ！四曲歌おうと思ってたんだけど、ちょっと一旦違うことするかのじゃ！
That was 'Wishing', noja! I was thinking of singing four songs, but I'm gonna do something else for a bit, noja!

204
00:27:30,134 --> 00:27:34,634
お主らはわしの英雄になってくれるのかなのじゃ！よし！
Will you all become my heroes, noja? Yosh!

205
00:27:35,134 --> 00:27:48,134
えっと、時間がないのじゃ！感謝をさせていただますのじゃ！どん！
Um, we don't have time, noja! Let me express my gratitude, noja! Bam!

206
00:27:48,134 --> 00:28:05,134
のじゃ！収益化大感謝ですのじゃ！優しくあたたかく応援してくれてるのめちゃくちゃ伝わってきてますのじゃ！
Noja! Thank you so much for the monetization celebration, noja! It really gets across how warmly and kindly you've been supporting me, noja!

207
00:28:05,134 --> 00:28:23,134
これからもいっぱいっぱい頑張るから見守ってくれたら嬉しいですのじゃ！ちょ、感謝のメッセージを置いておきつつ、ちょ、あと一曲歌おうと思ったんだけどじゃけど
I'll keep working hard, so I'd be so happy if you'd keep watching over me, noja! I'll leave my thank-you message here while... I was thinking of singing one more song, but...

208
00:28:23,134 --> 00:28:36,134
ちょ間に合わなさそうじゃから、ワンコーラスだけ最後に歌わせいただきますのじゃ！わしの時間管理ミスなのじゃ！おめンじらしすぎた！
...it doesn't look like we'll make it in time, so let me sing just one chorus at the end, noja! It was my time management mistake, noja! I teased you too much with the mask reveal!

209
00:28:36,134 --> 00:28:50,134
はい完全にめンじらしが長かったのじゃ！最後のいっきょく、ワンコーラスだけ歌わせてください！歌わせていただきますのじゃ！いよっ！えー聞いてください！シャイニースマリストーリー！
Yes, the mask reveal teasing was completely too long, noja! Please let me sing just one chorus of the final song! I'll sing it, noja! Here we go! Um, please listen! 'Shiny Smily Story'!

210
00:28:51,434 --> 00:28:55,434
同じ未来を見たいと
Wanting to see the same future,

211
00:28:55,934 --> 00:29:02,334
あの夢手にしたいそれぞれ違った
wanting to grasp that dream in our own different ways,

212
00:29:02,734 --> 00:29:09,634
ココロって走れGO!
run with all your heart, GO!

213
00:29:10,134 --> 00:29:15,134
今日は収益化記念お祝いしに来てくれてありがとなのじゃ！
Thank you so much for coming to celebrate my monetization today, noja!

214
00:29:16,634 --> 00:29:20,934
どこを見ても真っ暗な場所に芽生えてた
Sprouting in a pitch-black place no matter where I looked,

215
00:29:21,334 --> 00:29:25,634
ほんの小さな希望に
to a tiny little hope,

216
00:29:26,034 --> 00:29:32,234
この瞳奪われた不安で揺れる心をうまくチューニングして
my eyes were stolen, tuning my anxiously shaking heart,

217
00:29:32,834 --> 00:29:43,234
ほんの小さな勇気を振り絞っていたよ諦めの文字便利として進む苦しい時ももう私はひとりじゃないから
summoning up a tiny bit of courage. Even during painful times when resignation whispered to keep going, I'm no longer alone,

218
00:29:55,134 --> 00:29:59,634
だからもっと夢追いかけたい
so I want to chase my dreams even more.

219
00:30:00,310 --> 00:30:03,910
だからもっと夢 追いかけたい
That's why I want to chase my dreams even more...

220
00:30:04,110 --> 00:30:08,950
そう想像超えてく 世界見せてあげる
...and show you a world that goes beyond your imagination!

221
00:30:09,530 --> 00:30:14,490
アクセスしてみたい 後悔なんてさせない
I want you to access this, I won't let you regret it.

222
00:30:14,650 --> 00:30:22,670
それぞれ違った 心で走れ ゴー！
Run with different hearts, let's go!

223
00:30:23,390 --> 00:30:26,670
お主ら、今日は来てくれてありがとなのじゃ！
You guys, thank you so much for coming today!

224
00:30:26,950 --> 00:30:30,490
次はソピアの枠だそうなのじゃ！
Next up is Sopia's stream, they say!

225
00:30:30,890 --> 00:30:35,110
それでは、お主ら最後に挨拶するよ！
Alright everyone, time for our final greeting!

226
00:30:35,530 --> 00:30:38,430
せーの、さらばじゃー！
Ready, set—farewell!

227
00:30:40,091 --> 00:30:41,431
ありがとなのじゃ！
Thank you so much!

